            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present invention is directed to a garment comprising a base textile and a plurality of discrete film structures comprising a thermoplastic polyester elastomer affixed to the base textile, wherein upon exposure to moisture the plurality of discrete film structures undergoes a change in dimension in a direction that extends away from the surface of the garment in a positive or negative direction, and wherein areas of the base textile underlying the plurality of discrete film structures undergo a change in dimension in the direction that extends away from the surface of the garment in a positive or negative direction.</p>
            </abstract>
